+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

The uu-diff and uu-cmp commands use pledge(2) after resolving the
executable path and before reading input. The policy permits reading
files, including timezone data, and writing to inherited file
descriptors. The commands exit with status 2 if they cannot install the
policy.

The library entry points leave the policy of an embedding application
to its caller.
